later this month it will be one year  since the last american forces left  afghanistan ending a 20-year presence in  the country it was the longest war in  u.s history the government collapsed  when the taliban swept to power within  days mts taeyab is in kabul the capital  for a look at what has happened in the  last 12 months  good morning well a series of deadly  attacks over the past month is a massive  concern considering the relative peace  that followed the u.s withdrawal from  afghanistan and is perhaps a sign that  the taliban's grip on this country isn't  as tight as it seems  the horrifying aftermath of a suicide  bombing at a kabul mosque at least two  dozen were killed in the deadly attack  including the imam who was the apparent  target  is one of the survivors  i was attending evening prayer when the  explosion happened he says it was very  powerful and happened right inside the  mosque  as mourners buried loved ones the u.n  says the bombing is the latest in a  series of attacks which have killed and  injured more than 250 people in recent  weeks  the highest monthly number of civilian  casualties since the taliban's takeover  one year ago  the surge in violence comes as the  taliban celebrated the one-year  anniversary of its takeover of  afghanistan hundreds of heavily armed  olives and supporters filled this square  in central kabul not far from the now  abandoned u.s embassy  chanting god is great as taliban leaders  continue to transform afghanistan by  stripping women of basic rights barring  most high school-aged girls from  education and brutally cracking down on  any form of dissent despite the fact the  nation's economy has collapsed and is in  the grips of what the u.n is calling the  world's worst humanitarian disaster  at the rally we met abdullah sahami are  you happy with the taliban's leadership  no i'm not happy because  the economic problem is very  bad in afghanistan and also the  education is not  good  you know that the girl schools are  closed  so as the taliban celebrates one year on  the lives of ordinary afghans are  increasingly a misery  now no group has yet claimed  responsibility for the deadly mosque  attack but it follows a pattern that  we've seen with the afghan affiliate of  isis known as isis k  and the concern is is that the group  is only getting stronger  dana  all right mts thank you
 

